      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Choosing to take first use of an excellent early-season pitch, James Maycock dominated the Wadebridge innings in finally notching his first hundred for the club after a dozen County One fifties. Maycock's 110 featured 9x4s and 7x6s as he formed solid stands of 72 with fellow opener Matt Jolliffe (24) and 69 with Cal Morse (37) to give the Swans a platform for late over fireworks, which were duly provided by Barny Jackson (42) on his second club debut. Will Skene had the admirable figures of 2-25, while Mark Trudgeon bagged 2-60, although Wadebridge amassed a strong 271-8. In reply, Dean Burnett and Adam Trudgeon (37) built a solid first wicket platform, but from 71-0 Roche slid to 93-4, and despite Neil Trudgeon's quick 20 the hosts slipped behind the rate. Burnett was 7th out for a well compiled 72, but the last 6 wickets only added 23 as the visiting spinners sealed a 95-run victory, bowling Roche out for 176 in the 45th over, with Charlie Ellis (4-29) and Johnny Centini (2-43) among the late flurry of wickets.",
